Z||000000||count_iblis||01-07-2001||12:21 PM||||Ok, a friend of mine had a 85 gt.  Yesterday the car shifted fine and all. Well this morning he went to go to the store and the shifter was all loose and wouldnt even shift into gear.  there was like no gears to shift into.  what im trying to say is Iknow like in some transmissions that whne you try to go into gear it doesnt want to, this isnt the case it will go right up were it is suppose to but there seems like there isnt a gear.  COuld the shift cable be broke or something?  Need help.<P><BR>CHris<BR> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||JohnnyK||01-07-2001||12:58 PM||||If it just slides all over the place, it sounds like the shift cables broke. But overnight? Have someone watch the transmission and someone move the shift lever. If it's not moving, then it it something to do with the linkage (at the shifter) or the cables.||||reg||1
Z||000002||count_iblis||01-07-2001||01:11 PM||||so that dosent sound really bad then huh?  Not an expensive fix?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Greg Piet||01-07-2001||01:14 PM||||4speed Muncie eh?<BR>I had the same problem but it was stuck in 4th (same symptoms as my failure)<P>tranny rebuild, apparently a shaft/bolt in the tranny comes loose so the selector forks dont move properly...<P>I am not the guy to really answer this as I didnt repair it(had a shop do it), but if I were to guess...<P>Now I have a spare tranny ready to install if it happens again!<P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72<BR>#47 CSP<BR>Bring it to the track.<BR>Lets see if all those mods really helped!||||reg||1
